35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The monitors show one room draws four times the others. Sub-meters cost thirty-four thousand yen each. Precision has a price, and it’s steep.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, forty minutes a month is manageable! But keying in every invoice sounds exhausting. I’d rather not be the one doing that forever.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The rooms were assigned by lot, not need. That explains the heating gap. We should adjust for sunlight, not just raw usage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The statements show February at 29,400 yen, August at 9,100. No two months are close. I need to see the full yearly picture before committing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that late payments happened right after people felt confused. The money stress is making us avoid each other.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Jonathan, adjusting for sunlight is elegant, but the heater is the real culprit. We need a method that accounts for that specific, heavy draw without installing expensive meters.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, thirty-four thousand yen is way too much! @Jonathan, if we adjust for sunlight, does that make the math easier or harder?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It simplifies things. We weight the base cost by room exposure, then split the remainder equally. No meters needed, just fairness.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Jonathan, weighting by sunlight ignores the actual winter spike. I need to know the total annual cost and any upfront fees before I agree to this.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, the late payments show confusion hurts us. Maybe we can agree on a simple, kind way to share the winter costs?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, the winter spike is real, but it’s not a mystery. It’s just physics. We can model it without buying meters.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, I worry about the time cost! If the math is simple, maybe we can rotate who does it? I don’t want to be stuck with it forever.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, rotating the task prevents burnout. @Victoria, the annual total is fixed; the split just needs to reflect the physical reality of our rooms.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I cannot commit to a fixed split while winter costs remain unpredictable. I need the total annual figure and any upfront costs before agreeing.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I hear your worry, Victoria. The numbers are scary, but we can make them gentle. Let’s just agree to be patient with each other.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, the annual total is stable. The variance is seasonal, not chaotic. We can model the winter peak without buying expensive meters.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Benjamin"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Benjamin: Victoria, the annual total is stable. The variance is seasonal, not chaotic. We can model the winter peak without buying expensive meters.""}]}"
